rem Every Day Is a Holiday
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=645

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg D integer = 10000

rem A gap of one day between holidays
rem fills, longer gaps stay, so the year
rem is done once no two neighbouring
rem days (around the cycle) are both
rem birthday-free. With j days seen the
rem seen set is uniform, so state j is
rem still open with probability 1 - I(D,
rem D - j) / C(D, j), I(D, k) = D / (D -
rem k) C(D - k, k) the independent sets
rem of size k. State j costs D / (D - j)
rem draws, so E is the sum over the
rem k = D - j unseen days of (open) D / k.
Ks = 1 to D
Lg = ((1 to D) * 1.0) log
Lf = Lg scan + with 0.0
Km = Ks min (D // 2)
Lh = Lf (D - Km)
Lr = Lf (D - 2 * Km)
Ex = 2.0 * Lh - Lf D - Lr
Rt = Ex exp * D / (D - Km)
Ok = (Ks at most (D // 2)) integer
Rt = Rt * Ok
Tm = (1.0 - Rt) * D / Ks
Answer = (Tm sum) text ".4f"
Answer print
